  "notes": [
    "Every pin is 5 V tolerant on the F401. On the F411 two are not: PA0 and PB5 are 3.3 V only.",
    "The USB-C works out of the box, with the right D+ pull-up fitted. That alone is the reason to pick this over a Blue Pill.",
    "PC13 drives the blue LED and sinks it, so low turns it on. PC13, PC14 and PC15 are limited to 3 mA.",
    "There is a user button labeled KEY on PA0, active low. There is no debounce capacitor, so debounce it in software, and enable the internal pull-up. Holding BOOT0 at reset enters the built-in DFU bootloader over USB, so you can flash with dfu-util and no programmer at all.",
    "PA13 and PA14 are SWDIO and SWCLK on the 4-pin header at the bottom edge, not on the side headers.",
    "PA4, PA5, PA6 and PA7 also go to the optional on-board SPI flash footprint. If your board has the chip fitted, those four are shared.",
    "PB2 is BOOT1 and PC14 and PC15 carry the 32.768 kHz crystal, so treat all three as spoken for.",
    "On V3.1 boards the 5V header pins come from USB VBUS through a Schottky diode, so feeding 5 V in while USB is plugged in is safe. Older revisions may wire them straight to VBUS; check yours before back-feeding.",
    "Needs checking: the note that every pin is 5 V tolerant on the F401 version comes from WeAct's diagram. On the chip itself PC14, PC15, NRST and BOOT0 are not."
  ],
